(Northwind Support Escalation Policy) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Document ID: NW-SUP-2026-01) Tj
T*
(Effective date: 1 March 2026) Tj
T*
(Owner: Customer Support Leadership) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Severity definitions) Tj
T*
(   - SEV-1 \(Critical\): Production outage or data loss affecting many customers.) Tj
T*
(   - SEV-2 \(High\): Major feature unavailable with no practical workaround.) Tj
T*
(   - SEV-3 \(Medium\): Degraded experience with a workaround available.) Tj
T*
(   - SEV-4 \(Low\): Cosmetic issue or minor inconvenience.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Response time targets \(business hours, CET\)) Tj
T*
(   - SEV-1: first response within 15 minutes; update every 30 minutes.) Tj
T*
(   - SEV-2: first response within 1 hour; update every 2 hours.) Tj
T*
(   - SEV-3: first response within 1 business day.) Tj
T*
(   - SEV-4: first response within 3 business days.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Escalation path) Tj
T*
(   - Tier 1 Support acknowledges the ticket and triages severity.) Tj
T*
(   - Tier 2 Support owns SEV-2 and SEV-3 investigations.) Tj
T*
(   - On-call Engineering owns SEV-1 until mitigation.) Tj
T*
(   - Customer Success is notified for all SEV-1 accounts labeled Enterprise.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. After-hours coverage) Tj
T*
(   Only SEV-1 incidents page the on-call engineer outside business hours.) Tj
T*
(   SEV-2 and below wait until the next business day unless an Enterprise) Tj
T*
(   contract explicitly includes 24x7 coverage.) Tj
ET
